{"max_tokens":16384,"messages":[{"content":"Infer the grid transformation using only the explicitly observed outputs. Other input grids are public but their outputs are unknown. Do not assume unobserved outputs or reference solutions. Give four plausible contrasting mechanisms in named fields p0 through p3. Each should fit the observed examples and differ in an assumption that could change a prediction on another input. State the mechanism and distinguishing assumption, without asserting it is true. Do not merely rename one explanation. Use complete concise statements well within 512 characters per field. Previous proposals are fallible hypotheses, not additional observations. Revise their mechanisms using only listed observed outputs.","role":"system"},{"content":"{\"observations\": [{\"index\": 0, \"output\": [[9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 1, 5, 5, 5, 5, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 1, 5, 5, 5, 5], [9, 9, 9, 9, 1, 5, 5, 5, 5, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 1, 5, 5, 5, 5, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9], [9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 1, 5, 5, 5, 5, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 1, 5, 5, 5, 5], [9, 9, 9, 1, 5, 5, 5, 5, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 1, 5, 5, 5, 5, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9], [9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 1, 5, 5, 5, 5, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 1, 5, 5, 5, 5, 9, 9], [9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9], [9, 1, 5, 5, 5, 5, 9, 1, 5, 5, 5, 5, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 1, 5, 5, 5, 5, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9], [9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9], [9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 1, 5, 5, 5, 5, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 1, 5, 5, 5, 5, 9, 1, 5, 5, 5, 5], [1, 5, 5, 5, 5, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9], [9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 1, 5, 5, 5, 5, 9, 9, 9, 1, 5, 5, 5, 5, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9], [9, 1, 5, 5, 5, 5, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 1, 5, 5, 5, 5], [9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 1, 5, 5, 5, 5, 9, 1, 5, 5, 5, 5, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9], [9, 9, 1, 5, 5, 5, 5, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 1, 5, 5, 5, 5], [9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 1, 5, 5, 5, 5, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9], [9, 9, 9, 1, 5, 5, 5, 5, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 1, 5, 5, 5, 5, 9, 9], [9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9], [1, 5, 5, 5, 5, 9, 1, 5, 5, 5, 5, 9, 9, 1, 5, 5, 5, 5, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9], [9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 1, 5, 5, 5, 5, 9], [9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 1, 5, 5, 5, 5, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9], [9, 1, 5, 5, 5, 5, 9, 9, 9, 9, 1, 5, 5, 5, 5, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 1, 5, 5, 5, 5, 9, 9], [9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9], [9, 9, 1, 5, 5, 5, 5, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 1, 5, 5, 5, 5, 9, 1, 5, 5, 5, 5, 9, 9, 9, 9]]}], \"previous_proposals\": {\"plan\": {\"p0\": \"Replace every 2 with a centered five-cell horizontal object: [5,5,1,5,5], preserving all other cells. The distinguishing assumption is that every marker is independently active and the stamp may overwrite existing cells.\", \"p1\": \"Treat each 2 as the center of a left-anchored five-cell bar whose pattern is [1,5,5,5,5], as observed. Unlike p0, the stamp is clipped at borders and does not overwrite non-background cells; collisions retain the pre-existing object.\", \"p2\": \"Interpret the 2s as coordinates generated by a hidden horizontal-template layer. Reconstruct the template at every listed coordinate, but apply it only when the target five-cell span is entirely background; otherwise leave that marker unchanged. This differs on crowded or boundary cases.\", \"p3\": \"Use each 2 as a seed for a directional replacement: draw [1,5,5,5,5] with the 1 two columns left of the seed, but only for seeds belonging to the dominant background-colored component. Isolated seeds in a differently colored region would be ignored.\"}, \"slots\": [\"def transform(grid):\\n    h=len(grid); w=len(grid[0]) if h else 0\\n    out=[r[:] for r in grid]\\n    for r in range(h):\\n        for c in range(w):\\n            if grid[r][c]==2:\\n                for d,v in [(-2,5),(-1,5),(0,1),(1,5),(2,5)]:\\n                    q=c+d\\n                    if 0<=q<w: out[r][q]=v\\n    return out\", \"def transform(grid):\\n    h=len(grid); w=len(grid[0]) if h else 0\\n    out=[r[:] for r in grid]\\n    marks=[(r,c) for r in range(h) for c in range(w) if grid[r][c]==2]\\n    for r,c in marks:\\n        for d in range(-2,3):\\n            q=c+d\\n            if 0<=q<w:\\n                out[r][q]=1 if d==0 else 5\\n    return out\", \"def transform(grid):\\n    h=len(grid); w=len(grid[0]) if h else 0\\n    out=[r[:] for r in grid]\\n    bg=grid[0][0] if h and w else 0\\n    for r in range(h):\\n        for c in range(w):\\n            if grid[r][c]==2:\\n                for d,v in [(-2,1),(-1,5),(0,5),(1,5),(2,5)]:\\n                    q=c+d\\n                    if 0<=q<w and grid[r][q]==bg: out[r][q]=v\\n    return out\", \"def transform(grid):\\n    h=len(grid); w=len(grid[0]) if h else 0\\n    out=[r[:] for r in grid]\\n    bg=grid[0][0] if h and w else 0\\n    for r in range(h):\\n        for c in range(w):\\n            if grid[r][c]==2:\\n                for d,v in zip(range(-2,3),(5,5,1,5,5)):\\n                    q=c+d\\n                    if 0<=q<w and grid[r][q]==bg: out[r][q]=v\\n    return out\", \"def transform(grid):\\n    h=len(grid); w=len(grid[0]) if h else 0\\n    out=[r[:] for r in grid]\\n    bg=grid[0][0] if h and w else 0\\n    for r in range(h):\\n        for c in range(w):\\n            if grid[r][c]==2:\\n                qs=list(range(c-2,c+3))\\n                if all(0<=q<w and grid[r][q]==bg for q in qs):\\n                    for q,v in zip(qs,(1,5,5,5,5)): out[r][q]=v\\n    return out\", \"def transform(grid):\\n    h=len(grid); w=len(grid[0]) if h else 0\\n    out=[r[:] for r in grid]\\n    bg=grid[0][0] if h and w else 0\\n    runs=[]\\n    for r in range(h):\\n        c=0\\n        while c<w:\\n            if grid[r][c] not in (bg,2):\\n                s=c\\n                while c<w and grid[r][c] not in (bg,2): c+=1\\n                if c-s>=2: runs.append(grid[r][s:c])\\n            else: c+=1\\n    pat=max(runs,key=len) if runs else [1,5,5,5,5]\\n    if len(pat)>5: pat=pat[:5]\\n    for r in range(h):\\n        for c in range(w):\\n            if grid[r][c]==2:\\n                a=c-len(pat)//2; qs=list(range(a,a+len(pat)))\\n                if all(0<=q<w and grid[r][q]==bg for q in qs):\\n                    for q,v in zip(qs,pat): out[r][q]=v\\n    return out\", \"def transform(grid):\\n    h=len(grid); w=len(grid[0]) if h else 0\\n    out=[r[:] for r in grid]\\n    bg=grid[0][0] if h and w else 0\\n    pat=None\\n    for r in range(h):\\n        for c in range(w-4):\\n            x=grid[r][c:c+5]\\n            if all(v!=bg and v!=2 for v in x): pat=x; break\\n        if pat: break\\n    if pat is None: pat=[1,5,5,5,5]\\n    for r in range(h):\\n        for c in range(w):\\n            if grid[r][c]==2:\\n                a=c-2; qs=list(range(a,a+5))\\n                if all(0<=q<w and grid[r][q]==bg for q in qs):\\n                    for q,v in zip(qs,pat): out[r][q]=v\\n    return out\", \"def transform(grid):\\n    h=len(grid); w=len(grid[0]) if h else 0\\n    out=[r[:] for r in grid]\\n    if not h or not w: return out\\n    from collections import Counter\\n    bg=Counter(v for row in grid for v in row).most_common(1)[0][0]\\n    for r in range(h):\\n        for c in range(w):\\n            if grid[r][c]==2:\\n                a=c-2\\n                for q,v in zip(range(a,a+5),(1,5,5,5,5)):\\n                    if 0<=q<w and grid[r][q]==bg: out[r][q]=v\\n    return out\", \"def transform(grid):\\n    h=len(grid); w=len(grid[0]) if h else 0\\n    out=[row[:] for row in grid]\\n    for r in range(h):\\n        for c in range(w):\\n            if grid[r][c]==2:\\n                for k,v in enumerate((1,5,5,5,5)):\\n                    q=c-2+k\\n                    if 0<=q<w: out[r][q]=v\\n    return out\", \"def transform(grid):\\n    h=len(grid); w=len(grid[0]) if h else 0\\n    out=[row[:] for row in grid]\\n    marks=[(r,c) for r in range(h) for c in range(w) if grid[r][c]==2]\\n    for r,c in marks:\\n        for k,v in zip(range(-2,3),(1,5,5,5,5)):\\n            q=c+k\\n            if 0<=q<w: out[r][q]=v\\n    return out\", \"def transform(grid):\\n    h=len(grid); w=len(grid[0]) if h else 0\\n    out=[row[:] for row in grid]\\n    bg=grid[0][0] if h and w else 0\\n    for r in range(h):\\n        for c in range(w):\\n            if grid[r][c]==2:\\n                for k,v in enumerate((1,5,5,5,5)):\\n                    q=c-2+k\\n                    if 0<=q<w and grid[r][q]==bg: out[r][q]=v\\n    return out\", \"def transform(grid):\\n    h=len(grid); w=len(grid[0]) if h else 0\\n    out=[row[:] for row in grid]\\n    bg=grid[0][0] if h and w else 0\\n    for r in range(h):\\n        for c in range(w):\\n            if grid[r][c]==2:\\n                qs=list(range(c-2,c+3))\\n                if all(0<=q<w and grid[r][q]==bg for q in qs):\\n                    for q,v in zip(qs,(1,5,5,5,5)): out[r][q]=v\\n    return out\", \"def transform(grid):\\n    h=len(grid); w=len(grid[0]) if h else 0\\n    out=[row[:] for row in grid]\\n    bg=grid[0][0] if h and w else 0\\n    for r in range(h):\\n        for c in range(w):\\n            if grid[r][c]==2:\\n                qs=list(range(c-2,c+3))\\n                if all(0<=q<w and grid[r][q]==bg for q in qs):\\n                    for q,v in zip(qs,(1,5,5,5,5)): out[r][q]=v\\n    return out\", \"def transform(grid):\\n    h=len(grid); w=len(grid[0]) if h else 0\\n    out=[row[:] for row in grid]\\n    bg=grid[0][0] if h and w else 0\\n    for r in range(h):\\n        for c in range(w):\\n            if grid[r][c]==2:\\n                a=c-2\\n                if all(0<=q<w and grid[r][q]==bg for q in range(a,a+5)):\\n                    for q,v in zip(range(a,a+5),(1,5,5,5,5)): out[r][q]=v\\n    return out\", \"def transform(grid):\\n    h=len(grid); w=len(grid[0]) if h else 0\\n    out=[row[:] for row in grid]\\n    if not h or not w: return out\\n    bg=grid[0][0]\\n    seen=set(); stack=[(0,0)]\\n    while stack:\\n        r,c=stack.pop()\\n        if (r,c) in seen or not (0<=r<h and 0<=c<w) or grid[r][c]!=bg: continue\\n        seen.add((r,c))\\n        stack += [(r-1,c),(r+1,c),(r,c-1),(r,c+1)]\\n    for r in range(h):\\n        for c in range(w):\\n            if grid[r][c]==2 and any((r, q) in seen for q in range(max(0,c-2),min(w,c+3))):\\n                for k,v in enumerate((1,5,5,5,5)):\\n                    q=c-2+k\\n                    if 0<=q<w and grid[r][q]==bg: out[r][q]=v\\n    return out\", \"def transform(grid):\\n    h=len(grid); w=len(grid[0]) if h else 0\\n    out=[row[:] for row in grid]\\n    if not h or not w: return out\\n    from collections import Counter\\n    bg=Counter(x for row in grid for x in row).most_common(1)[0][0]\\n    for r in range(h):\\n        for c in range(w):\\n            if grid[r][c]==2:\\n                for k,v in enumerate((1,5,5,5,5)):\\n                    q=c-2+k\\n                    if 0<=q<w and grid[r][q]==bg: out[r][q]=v\\n    return out\"]}, \"public_inputs\": [[[9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 2, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 2, 9, 9], [9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 2, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 2, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9], [9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 2, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 2, 9, 9], [9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 2, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 2, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9], [9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 2, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 2, 9, 9, 9, 9], [9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9], [9, 9, 9, 2, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 2, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 2, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9], [9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9], [9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 2, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 2, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 2, 9, 9], [9, 9, 2, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9,